  "final": "`get_document` and `list_documents` now only return documents that match both the tenant and the owner and haven't been deleted. Both existing checks and a new access check pass.\n\n**Changes:**\n- **`src/repository.py`**:\n  - `find` now takes `tenant` and `owner` and adds `tenant=? AND owner=? AND deleted_at IS NULL` to its query, all as bound parameters.\n  - `listing` now takes `tenant` as well as `owner`, applies the same filters and still sorts by `id`.\n  - Results still contain only `id`, `title` and `body`, so no deletion metadata comes back. If a document is in another tenant, belongs to another owner, is deleted or doesn't exist, `get_document` returns the same `None` in every case.\n- **`src/service.py`**: passes `tenant` and `owner` through to the repository functions. The function signatures haven't changed.\n- **`checks/access.py`** (new) covers:\n  - cross-tenant, cross-owner, deleted and missing IDs all returning `None`\n  - lists excluding those records and staying sorted by `id`\n  - tenant and owner names containing `'` and `\"` working correctly\n  - injection-style inputs like `t' OR '1'='1` returning nothing\n\n**Note:** `find` and `listing` now take extra parameters. Nothing else in the project calls them, but any outside code that does would need updating.",
